==Latin==

===Etymology===
According to LIV, from {{der|la|ine-pro|*snewbʰ-||to marry, to wed}}.<ref>{{R:ine:LIV|head=*snewbʰ-}}</ref> Ernout and Meillet instead connect this word with {{m|la|nūbēs||cloud}}, from PIE {{m|ine-pro|*(s)newdʰ-||to cover}}.<ref>{{R:la:EM|page=449}}</ref> De Vaan finds this semantically attractive but morphologically difficult: if the supine stem is old it cannot reflect stem-final ''*dʰ''.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|head=nūbō|page=417}}</ref> Possibly cognate with {{cog|grc|νύμφη||bride, young wife, nymph}} (English {{m|en|nymph}}), but this is disputed.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|nūbō}}

===Verb===
{{la-verb|3|nūbō|nūps|nūpt}}

# {{lb|la|intransitive|+ [[Appendix:Glossary#dative case|dative]]}} I get married to, [[marry]], [[wed]] (for a woman).
# {{lb|la|intransitive|of plants}} I become joined, tied or [[wedded]] to.
# {{lb|la|transitive|rare}} I [[cover]], [[veil]].
#; {{syn|la|velo|obnubo|occulto|occulo|indūcō|recondo|adoperio|verrō|condo}}

